Step 1: Understand the Core Concepts
Before writing any configuration files, you need to understand the problems CI/CD solves.
Continuous Integration (CI): The practice of automating the building and testing of your code every time a developer commits a change. 
This catches bugs early before they reach production.
Continuous Delivery / Deployment (CD): Taking the successfully tested code and automatically packaging it.
Delivery prepares the code to be deployed at the click of a button.Deployment pushes it to live servers automatically without human intervention.
